# check_disk_instability with R3's flags (FIREmodeOn 1, R3.par:55; SFprescription 1, BulgeSizeOn 3, every other flag and parameter R2.par's) on a real R3 central at Snap_63
# with its cold gas raised by a factor 1.25: gas-unstable, so the continuation (R/src/model_disk_instability.c:90-108) grows the
# black hole and bursts the unstable fraction (mode 1) with SAGE26's FIRE budget from
# the galaxy's own float Vvir and stored-snapshot redshift (observed, nested_burst_fire_*);
# MassLoading left unchanged.
# galaxy 0: R3 reference /Volumes/Internal/results/sage26-campaign/workspace/e01-reference/out/R3/model_0.hdf5 (SHA-256 ab278992616f7137b526e5bd3a43045f2e753e29d84997fc69350255c38f570c), Snap_63 row 33 (GalaxyIndex 121, Type 0)
# End-of-snapshot output values used as plausible call inputs, not reconstructed call-time
# state (DiskScaleRadius is the output's DiskRadius; MassLoading the row's stale value).
# Constructed: ColdGas and MetalsColdGas raised (a plausible call-time inflow; the row and
# factor chosen by build.py's tune so the quasar wind before the burst leaves cold gas),
# the stored
# SnapNum (the output snapshot) and ZZ[SnapNum] = 1/AA - 1, OutflowRate 0 and zero
# histories, as at substep 0; the timing is the R2 template's.
# Reachability: R3-reachable.
format sage26-oracle-fixture 1
routine check_disk_instability_fire

i32 params.SFprescription 1  # R3 (R3.par:48): BR06 with radial integration
